# Maintainer: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
#
# The Flutter engine for Linux desktop on ppc64le (POWER8+, little-endian,
# ELFv2, glibc): libflutter_linux_gtk.so, gen_snapshot and the host tools for
# the debug, profile and release runtime modes, installed where the flutter
# tool looks for them (package `flutter`). It is built from the flutter/flutter
# monorepo at the release tag, with its own copy of the Dart VM, which carries
# the ppc64 port.
#
# With the native ppc64 Dart backend (JIT and AOT), 2026-11-19: debug,
# profile and release build and run natively, no simulator. The engine
# track's report (flutter-port work/engine/REPORT-NATIVE.md) has the
# measurements this recipe reproduces: the engine unit tests and the
# engine's testing/dart suite under flutter_tester match the simarm64
# reference, and a release libapp.so runs through the GTK embedder.
#
# Class: local workaround (distribution packaging: system toolchain and
# libraries, no gclient, CIPD client or sysroot). The ppc64 enablement it
# carries is classified patch by patch, in each patch's Class: line.
#
# Seven things about this build are worth knowing before changing it.
#
# 1. SOURCES ARE FETCHED IN prepare(), SHALLOW, BY COMMIT ID. The monorepo is
#    fetched at $_commit and the 81 git DEPS (71 top level + 10 from
#    vulkan-deps) by fetch-flutter-deps, which lives beside this file (as
#    chromium's fetch-chromium-release does): one `git fetch --depth 1 <url>
#    <sha>` each, then checked against its pin. Measured 2026-11-19: all of
#    prepare() (fetch, patches, gates, hooks) takes 78-85 s, and the shallow
#    .git directories total 0.6 GiB. The other way is one makepkg
#    `name::git+url#commit=` source per repo, which is makepkg's
#    `git clone --mirror` (source/git.sh): full history and every ref, kept
#    in SRCDEST. Measured for the 8 biggest of the 82 repos alone: 18.6 GiB
#    and 26 min (8 clones in parallel) against 0.41 GiB shallow: dart 5.2 GiB
#    (382,690 refs), skia 4.2 GiB (370,287 refs), swiftshader 4.0 GiB, the
#    monorepo 2.8 GiB, icu 1.3 GiB, boringssl 0.7 GiB, angle and
#    flutter_packages 0.2 GiB each. What git+ would buy: no network on a
#    rebuild once SRCDEST is warm (bq deletes its work tree after a build, so
#    this recipe refetches 0.6 GiB each time), and a complete
#    `makepkg --allsource`. A side effect to know about: content_aware_hash.sh
#    treats a non-shallow detached checkout as a development branch and
#    hashes at the merge-base with origin/master (harmless; that hash is only
#    used for Android).
#    Either way the engine's tools/gn needs real git checkouts: it runs
#    `git rev-parse HEAD` in engine/src/flutter, third_party/skia and
#    third_party/dart for engine_version, skia_version, dart_version and
#    the Dart SDK hash. A tag tarball would not do.
#    bq shares the host's network namespace (flutter-port R15), so fetching
#    in prepare() works under bq. The two CIPD packages are ordinary
#    checksummed source=() entries, taken from CIPD's plain /dl/ endpoint.
#
# 2. TWO PATCH SERIES, BOTH FLAT, BOTH GATED.
#    - The engine series (NNNN-*.patch beside this file, applied with
#      `patch -p1` at the monorepo root, so a patch can reach a DEPS
#      checkout such as libpng with ordinary paths). The series' durable
#      home is this directory.
#    - The Dart port series (dart-NNNN-*.patch). These are SYMLINKS into the
#      `dart` recipe's directory, made by ./sync-dart-series. The series has
#      one home, beside dart's PKGBUILD. The engine applies it to
#      engine/src/flutter/third_party/dart, which is the same commit as
#      dart's tag (c70f78e7). One kind of Dart patch is skipped: a patch
#      that touches only a Dart DEPS checkout which the engine supplies at a
#      different path, matched by path, never by number. Today that is
#      BoringSSL (dart's target.h patch); engine 0012 is the same change,
#      hunk for hunk.
#    The Dart series is applied UNCOMMITTED, on the tag: third_party/dart's
#    HEAD stays at c70f78e7. tools/make_version.py bakes `git rev-parse
#    --short=10 HEAD` into the VM as its SDK hash, so a commit there would
#    give a hash the `dart` package does not have, and the flutter tool fails
#    with "Unexpected Kernel SDK Version" (engine REPORT-NATIVE 2). The GN
#    arg dart_sdk_verification_hash pins the kernel tools' side too, and
#    build() gates that every staged .dill header, every engine binary and
#    the dart package agree on c70f78e7d6 (and verify_sdk_hash stays on).
#    Gates, in the dart recipe's style. Each one hashes a tree with git
#    (`add -A -f; write-tree`), with every DEPS path excluded:
#      gate 1  the monorepo is the tag (_base_tree)
#      gate D  third_party/dart after the Dart series == _dart_tree, which is
#              `dart`'s _tree. This proves the engine embeds the same Dart
#              source as the dart package (BoringSSL aside, see above).
#      gate 2  the monorepo after the engine series == _tree
#      deps    each DEPS checkout the series touches == _dep_trees[path]
#
# 3. TOOLCHAIN: SYSTEM ONLY. clang/lld/llvm through clang_base_path="/usr"
#    (engine 0002), the pool's gn (>= 2489; 0.2595 in the pool, the one
#    chromium uses, with engine 0009's strict-include opt-out), the system
#    ninja and python, no sysroot (--no-default-linux-sysroot, system gtk3,
#    glib2 and pango). No CIPD, no depot_tools, no prebuilt clang.
#    -faltivec-src-compat=mixed is pinned through engine 0014 and asserted on
#    every ppc64 compile: clang warns that its default will become "xl", which
#    makes vector compares scalar (engine REPORT 8.4). Measured 2026-11-19:
#    mixed, today's default, is the only mode in which Skia's skcms compiles
#    at all; "gcc", which the engine track suggested, and "xl" both fail.
#
# 4. THE PREBUILT DART IS THE POOL'S `dart` PACKAGE, AS A LEAF. The engine's
#    GN graph runs third_party/dart/tools/sdks/dart-sdk/bin/dart from
#    build/gn_run_binary.py, and so do the DEPS hooks. That runs the
#    front end (compile_platform, kernel compiles, sdk_rewriter), never
#    machine-code generation: snapshots are made by the gen_snapshot this
#    build compiles. tools/sdks/dart-sdk is a symlink to /usr/lib/dart
#    (_driver=system, the default: 1.8x faster than the emulated bootstrap at
#    the same kernel compile, REPORT-NATIVE 8.6); _driver=bootstrap uses
#    /usr/lib/dart-bootstrap. The CONTROL checks refuse anything that is not
#    a native linux_ppc64 Dart from the right pool, and refuse a build graph
#    that runs an out-of-tree binary or names an upstream or bootstrap SDK
#    path. The `dart` package is a makedepend either way: its PRODUCT
#    frontend_server_aot.dart.snapshot replaces the engine-built one in
#    linux-ppc64/, as upstream ships it. The engine's is built by its own
#    non-product gen_snapshot, and a product runtime refuses it
#    ("dedup_instructions is false in snapshot", REPORT-NATIVE 6).
#
# 5. CODEGEN IS POWER8 IN BOTH POOLS, C++ IS PER POOL. Dart's backend has no
#    ISA 3.0 emitter, so gen_snapshot output (every app's libapp.so) is ISA
#    2.07 whichever pool built it. _power8_compat selects only the C/C++
#    -mcpu/-mtune of the engine itself, through the GN arg ppc64_cpu (GN
#    never reads CFLAGS, so makepkg.conf.d/00-power8.conf cannot reach this
#    build). build() asserts that -mcpu=<want> -mtune=<want> reach every
#    C/C++ compile and that no other -mcpu/-mtune is named anywhere in the
#    graph. ISA policy, as in the dart recipe: AOT outputs (the staged
#    frontend_server_aot snapshot and a libapp.so that build() compiles with
#    the release gen_snapshot) carry 0 ISA 3.0 instructions in BOTH pools,
#    scanned over the whole .text with objdump -D -z -j .text, a coverage
#    floor and a mid-.text control (isa30-text-scan.py; a stripped libapp.so
#    defeats plain -d, NOTES item 17). Native ELFs are counted in the POWER9
#    pool; in the baseline pool any ISA 3.0 instruction must lie in libgcc's
#    IFUNC'd IEEE-128 *_hw routines (isa30-attribute.py, shared with dart),
#    and the engine links libgcc_s dynamically, so 0 is what to expect.
#
# 6. bq RUNS makepkg --nocheck. Every gate is in prepare() or build(); check()
#    only runs in a native by-hand build, where it builds and runs the
#    engine's own test suites (see check()). Inside bq, /usr is a read-only
#    overlay and $HOME is the real home, so prepare() and build() point HOME,
#    PUB_CACHE and XDG_CONFIG_HOME into $srcdir. package() runs under
#    fakeroot and only copies files. It never runs a Dart, and never an
#    emulated binary of any kind: POWERarm cannot reach its server as uid 0.
#
# 7. BUILD THIS NATIVELY: through bq / tools/build-ppc64le.sh, or makepkg in a
#    native shell. Never build it from inside the POWERarm aarch64 sleeve that
#    Claude sessions run in. There fakeroot half-works and produces
#    -rw------- packages owned by the builder. An agent reaches the native
#    shell with: ssh -n -i ~/.ssh/id_claude_omarchy -o BatchMode=yes localhost
#    Put the build root on /mnt/arch (BQ_BUILDROOT): the tree is ~5 GiB before
#    the three out/ directories.
#
# PKGREL RULE. Bump pkgrel whenever the Dart series changes at the same
# pkgver (the engine embeds that VM), and whenever this recipe's own patches
# or gates change. Bump localsend after any engine change: its bundle copies
# libflutter_linux_gtk.so.
#
# THE ENGINE SERIES (the Dart series' classes are in the dart recipe's
# header; its files are the dart-NNNN-* symlinks here). 0001-0013 are the
# engine track's patches-native (work/engine, tools/verify-series reproduces
# their trees); 0014 is this recipe's.
#   0001 [engine] Backport: riscv64 desktop linux engine     -- upstream backport
#   0002 [engine] ppc64 (LE ELFv2) desktop Linux host        -- upstreamable in form; local
#   0003 [engine] build: treat_warnings_as_errors arg        -- upstreamable fix
#   0004 [engine] tools/gn: python3 when no vpython3         -- upstreamable fix
#   0005 [engine] build: the missing get_host_byteorder.py   -- upstreamable fix
#   0006 [engine] fml/tonic/assets: ppc64le CPU tables       -- upstreamable in form; local
#   0007 [engine] Backport: GTK embedder on Pango 1.58.0     -- upstream backport
#   0008 [engine] linux: glib.h before extern "C" ATK        -- upstreamable fix
#   0009 [engine] build: opt out of strict include checking  -- local workaround (gn >= 2591)
#   0010 [engine] lib/snapshot: gen_snapshot, analyze_snapshot for ppc64
#                                                            -- upstreamable in form; local
#   0011 [libpng] BUILD.gn: portable filters on ppc64        -- upstreamable fix
#   0012 [boringssl] target.h: ppc64le, portable C           -- upstreamable fix in spirit;
#                                                               local (== dart's patch)
#   0013 [swiftshader] MC XCOFF base classes for LLVM PPC    -- upstreamable fix
#   0014 [engine] build: pin -faltivec-src-compat=mixed      -- upstreamable fix (guard)

pkgname=flutter-engine
pkgver=3.41.9
pkgrel=1
pkgdesc='Flutter engine for Linux desktop: libflutter_linux_gtk.so, gen_snapshot and host tools, debug/profile/release (ppc64le port)'
arch=('powerpc64le')
url='https://flutter.dev'
license=('BSD-3-Clause')

_url=https://github.com/flutter/flutter.git
_commit=00b0c91f06209d9e4a41f71b7a512d6eb3b9c694       # tag 3.41.9
_commit_time='Wed Apr 29 17:03:19 2026 +0000'           # git log -1 --format=%cd 3.41.9
# The tag's tree: git rev-parse 3.41.9^{tree}.
_base_tree=77bb2e2312ad0f9cdf8e44d868396dc3751b1ed8
# bin/internal/engine.version at the tag: the content-aware hash the flutter
# tool keys its engine stamps on. Recorded in .pkginfo for the tool package.
_engine_revision=42d3d75a56efe1a2e9902f52dc8006099c45d937
# The Dart inside: DEPS dart_revision, which is dart's tag 3.11.5.
_dart_pkgver=3.11.5
_dart_commit=c70f78e7d682c158c15ca0c26c729b3ccb932284

# Gate 2: the monorepo after the engine series, DEPS paths excluded, measured
# by this recipe's prepare() from a fresh fetch, 2026-11-19. Without 0014 the
# same tree is cf4a819f, the engine track's patches-native monorepo tree
# (tools/verify-series), so 0001-0013 are exactly the engine track's.
_tree=2178c90b4fbad37a605aff2414dc5cc30e183736
# Gate D: third_party/dart after the Dart series, DEPS paths excluded. It must
# equal the dart recipe's _tree (sync-dart-series keeps them equal): C's
# ppc64-backend tree, which the engine track's import also reproduced.
_dart_tree=c5aba92a8a98e5187a38d8942ffac4b1f186d428
# DEPS checkouts the engine series patches, after patching, by path. -g:
# makepkg sources this file inside a function.
declare -gA _dep_trees=(
  [engine/src/flutter/third_party/libpng]=b29bb83c3d49aa8e312a26e240c7ac351caba15d        # 0011
  [engine/src/flutter/third_party/boringssl/src]=a67ee71bb8c93180b9f6c516bcc92702db6b5b7a # 0012 (== dart's)
  [engine/src/flutter/third_party/swiftshader]=007aa2a50d0c3eaff8b56027e42cc8de56bebb78   # 0013
  # dart-lang/native inside the engine's Dart (same pin, 9a115379, as the
  # dart recipe's): the Dart series patches it (Architecture.ppc64, ABI-SPEC
  # A2). Gate D excludes it as a DEPS path, so it is gated here, against the
  # dart recipe's _dep_trees[third_party/pkg/native]. The interim engine 0013
  # and its third_party/dart entry are gone (2026-11-19): the full Dart series
  # carries the TARGET_ARCH_PPC64 GN wiring and analyze_snapshot itself.
  [engine/src/flutter/third_party/dart/third_party/pkg/native]=6b5e0cd25a6572ab51fb683632a2995c3dad5db1
)

# Dart patches whose every path lies under one of these Dart DEPS paths are
# skipped here: the engine's DEPS supplies that checkout elsewhere and the
# engine series carries the change (BoringSSL -> engine 0012, the same hunks;
# its tree equals the dart recipe's BoringSSL gate). A Dart patch that mixes such a path with others is an
# error.
_dart_relocated=('third_party/boringssl/src')

_devtools_rev=9be2c887e3982e519cf58f185d5f7b008a4606e9
_fonts_iid=44bd38be0bc8c189a397ca6dd6f737746a9e0c6117b96a8f84f1edf6acd1206b

# Measured DT_NEEDED of the native build's staged ELFs (all three modes,
# 2026-11-19): libflutter_linux_gtk.so needs gtk-3, gdk-3, pangocairo, atk,
# pango, cairo, gio/gobject/glib, epoxy, fontconfig, libgcc_s and glibc;
# flutter_tester fontconfig, libgcc_s, glibc; impellerc libgcc_s, glibc;
# gen_snapshot, font-subset, libpath_ops.so, libtessellator.so glibc only.
depends=('gtk3' 'pango' 'at-spi2-core' 'cairo' 'glib2' 'libepoxy' 'fontconfig' 'libgcc' 'glibc')
# Present on the host 2026-11-19: gn 0.2595, clang/lld 22.1.8, llvm 22.1.8,
# ninja 1.13.2, python 3.14.7, git 2.55, gtk3 3.24.52. The linux embedder's
# pkg-config set is gtk+-3.0, epoxy, egl and x11
# (shell/platform/linux/config/BUILD.gn).
makedepends=('gn>=0.2595' 'clang' 'lld' 'llvm' 'ninja' 'python' 'git' 'patch'
             'file' 'binutils' 'gtk3' 'libepoxy' 'libglvnd' 'libx11' 'fontconfig'
             "dart=$_dart_pkgver")
# check() only: GTK on broadway inside a private D-Bus with the AT-SPI bus,
# Xvfb + Mesa for the GLES backend of impeller_unittests, cc for the nodump
# preload.
checkdepends=('dbus' 'at-spi2-core' 'gtk3' 'xorg-server-xvfb' 'xorg-xauth' 'mesa' 'gcc')
# !strip: the build already strips what upstream ships stripped, and
# frontend_server_aot.dart.snapshot is an ELF written by Dart's own ELF writer
# that strip would treat as a library. !lto: GN ignores makepkg's flags.
options=('!strip' '!debug' '!lto')

# --- POWER8 / POWER9 ---------------------------------------------------------
# Set by tools/build-ppc64le.sh for the baseline pool. Selects ppc64_cpu (the
# engine's C/C++ -mcpu) and which pool's dart-bootstrap the CONTROL accepts.
_power8_compat=${_power8_compat:-0}

# --- which Dart runs the front-end actions -----------------------------------
#   system     /usr/lib/dart, the pool's own dart package (default)
#   bootstrap  /usr/lib/dart-bootstrap
_driver=${_driver:-system}
case $_driver in
  system)    _driver_sdk=/usr/lib/dart ;;
  bootstrap) _driver_sdk=/usr/lib/dart-bootstrap; makedepends+=("dart-bootstrap=$_dart_pkgver") ;;
  *)         _driver_sdk= ;;   # prepare() refuses
esac
# The dart package itself: its product frontend_server snapshot is staged, and
# its SDK hash is the one every engine artifact must carry.
_dart_sdk=/usr/lib/dart
_dart_sdk_hash=c70f78e7d6   # dart 3.11.5's tag, git rev-parse --short=10

